701 1113 #uuid "0685e1c6-7326-51d7-82c2-83d6b3ede4ef" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381701 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{(2)({x}^{2}-1)-(2x)(2x)}{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}-2-4{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(1+{x}^{2})}{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all real values of $x,$ with $x\\ne \\pm 1.$ So there is no solution for ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ \n\nSo, the only critical points are the endpoints $x=3,5$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =\\frac{2(3)}{(3)^{2}-1}=\\frac{6}{8}=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ f(5) & =\\frac{2(5)}{(5)^{2}-1}=\\frac{10}{24}=\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(3)=\\frac{3}{4},$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(5)=\\frac{5}{12},$ so the global minimum is $\\frac{5}{12}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075289/assets/14747ab1b46e589f0692d9e3dc5ffbe91eb1d60e3641d47d1a5eacb5f1df1130.png)" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381703 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381704 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381705 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381706 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381707 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1041 "selection" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381706 13194139536062 true] [17592186381702 1110 #uuid "0577fe80-4ecc-52cc-9b93-316d000ed2ff" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381703 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381703 1111 #uuid "3a4bf96e-7ac6-59a6-bab8-4631fcb3d9bc" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381704 1034 "\\frac{5}{12}" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381704 1111 #uuid "80c41a44-d3b4-5185-ac2d-a7ead1480144" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381705 1034 "3" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381705 1111 #uuid "e26c594b-d766-549d-8475-f3151f2d0eae" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381706 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381706 1111 #uuid "50eb51f1-f87d-598d-86b9-78839b90cff5" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381707 1034 "4" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381707 1111 #uuid "5deaa947-60af-5427-80bc-7fde7faf3ed7" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381708 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381709 13194139536062 true] [17592186381708 1089 "q-22615" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381708 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536062 true] [17592186381708 1100 "For the function $f(x)=x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ defined on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le \\pi ,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\sqrt{3}$\n- The global maximum value is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\sqrt{3}$\n- The global minimum value is $0$" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381708 1113 #uuid "d3d1d570-9705-5d73-82f5-b8bee8639610" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381708 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n,\\,\\,\\,\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer. We discard all solutions except $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ since it is the only value that belongs to the given interval.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ and the endpoints $x=0,\\pi $ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =0+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0 \\\\ f(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\sqrt{3}≈3.8 \\\\ f(\\pi ) & =\\pi +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=\\pi ≈3.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\sqrt{3},$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(0)=0,$ so the global minimum is $0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075289/assets/539dc4ccd2f1b20f521ae0f70bb5d95b8c5f9d1a006ff102baf43ac13ce19660.png)" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381710 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381711 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381712 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381713 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381714 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1041 "selection" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381710 13194139536062 true] [17592186381709 1110 #uuid "c693db04-4e68-5288-bd55-043640c57719" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381710 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381710 1111 #uuid "ced4697d-765a-529d-a4dd-00f4dafdf98e" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381711 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381711 1111 #uuid "80fe567f-8313-57c8-a1e9-a987c3ad37de" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381712 1034 "I only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381712 1111 #uuid "d6ae36bc-22f7-5c23-a87e-5447737387ce" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381713 1034 "III only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381713 1111 #uuid "5e21c718-0110-5de8-a336-f3fd0076f9ee" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381714 1034 "II only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381714 1111 #uuid "cf668686-0ec1-5c92-85e4-4a0b1546ca2c" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381715 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381716 13194139536062 true] [17592186381715 1089 "q-2691" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381715 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536062 true] [17592186381715 1100 "For the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+4,$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $4$\n- The global maximum value is $2$\n- The global minimum value is $0$" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381715 1113 #uuid "d05c5e81-6be8-59d5-ab47-d0e86e875c97" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381715 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-6x \\\\  & =2x(2{x}^{2}-3),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n2x(2{x}^{2}-3)=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.\n$$\n\nSince $x=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}$ do not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1)^{4}-3(-1)^{2}+4=2 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{4}-3(0)^{2}+4=4 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{4}-3(1)^{2}+4=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=4,$ so the global maximum is $4.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-1)=f(1)=2,$ so the global minimum is $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075289/assets/a7141a342d971d5b520b2f7f07f8fdb1c01ddca18a983fb0c83102a5bd4aee8e.png)" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381717 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381718 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381719 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381720 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381721 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1041 "selection" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381719 13194139536062 true] [17592186381716 1110 #uuid "c9f2ee4e-8955-53e8-86ec-4364035cbbfe" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381717 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381717 1111 #uuid "dd40f474-1dd7-531e-a6b9-75f2cbd9d8c5" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381718 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381718 1111 #uuid "bea2f439-8a1e-5005-acec-6526275fb0ee" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381719 1034 "I only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381719 1111 #uuid "be573206-7ab8-5025-9584-395733e6cb27" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381720 1034 "III only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381720 1111 #uuid "0ae1905a-e5c1-5d29-a23d-2e5881b5d875" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381721 1034 "II only" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536062 true] [17592186381721 1111 #uuid "f48dd62e-c1b7-5701-874f-e853928e35eb" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381722 1034 "1" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381722 1111 #uuid "bebb93d0-8f13-5c5f-ab86-c1fde0abceb2" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381723 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381724 13194139536062 true] [17592186381723 1089 "q-344464" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536062 true] [17592186381723 1100 "The exact global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}-x$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 2$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139536062 true] [17592186381723 1113 #uuid "5a631e09-e1d1-50ec-bbed-e44b79c9b773" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381723 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}-x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+4}}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+4}}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+4}} & =1 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{x+4} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+4} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x+4 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-\\frac{15}{4}$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,2],$ the critical points are the endpoints $x=-1,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =\\sqrt{-1+4}-(-1)=\\sqrt{3}+1 \\\\ f(2) & =\\sqrt{2+4}-2=\\sqrt{6}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-1)=\\sqrt{3}+1,$ so the global maximum is $\\sqrt{3}+1.$\n\n- The least value is $f(2)=\\sqrt{6}-2,$ so the global minimum is $\\sqrt{6}-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075289/assets/ade599dd27bc3d018a3604620f3741ae05f8ebcc8ff583994da155ce7f311146.png)" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381725 13194139536062 true] [17592186381724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536062 true] [17592186381724 1041 "field-1" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381725 13194139536062 true] [17592186381724 1110 #uuid "8776dca8-a97f-5180-8c28-51a7954bf1fd" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381725 1034 "\\sqrt{3}+1" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381725 1111 #uuid "15c7c45c-ad4a-575a-adc2-18e6e78bc781" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381726 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381727 13194139536062 true] [17592186381726 1089 "q-344477" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381726 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536062 true] [17592186381726 1100 "The exact global maximum value of the function $f(x)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le \\pi $ is{{field-1}}." 13194139536062 true] [17592186381726 1113 #uuid "42ea67fe-58dc-59cf-90b1-7bed8af018d8" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381726 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & =0 \\\\ 2x & =\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer. We discard all solutions except $x=0,$ $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ and $x=\\pi ,$ since they are the only values that belong to the given interval.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\pi ,$ and the endpoints $x=0,\\,\\pi $ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0 \\\\ f\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=1-(-1)=2 \\\\ f(\\pi ) & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=2,$ so the global maximum is $2.$\n\n- The least value is $f(0)=0,$ so the global minimum is $0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075289/assets/6b8ac504d93007049795ee92eb8865225751314478d68ace67878e27ed471b24.png)" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381728 13194139536062 true] [17592186381727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381729 13194139536062 true] [17592186381727 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536062 true] [17592186381727 1041 "field-1" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381727 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381728 13194139536062 true] [17592186381727 1110 #uuid "17bc309a-4946-559c-8ac4-4407812e6d91" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381728 1034 "2" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381728 1111 #uuid "a76a859a-c6f2-510e-a346-641b648f5445" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381729 1034 "0" 13194139536062 true] [17592186381729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536062 true] [17592186381729 1111 #uuid "48d95e5e-390a-5265-a123-55f754215771" 13194139536062 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-113769" 17592186381694 "q-113769/selection" 17592186381695 "q-113769/selection/2ebfdfa167dbe8c7503b59814041a90f4394641c529f5bbe28427626a54631a1" 17592186381696 "q-113769/selection/5db43cd11478876feefa32cc3f6c8505391b913fe1f94a080ae3cc7e54460f77" 17592186381697 "q-113769/selection/a1b2ccfba458a845fd8ee10e6daa31506496a50a50042e082232a7d8cf1de62a" 17592186381698 "q-113769/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" 17592186381699 "q-113769/selection/efeed6473f4b47114805fa9c2f59cd6c